\pard\b\fs20 The War of Faith\b0\par
\fs16\par
Since the year 80 after Barius, the two churches, the Order of Sawel\'f4 and the Legion of Teiwaz, have plunged Meduvia into a terrible war. No farming village is safe from their clashes. The two gods try ever new means to strengthen their party and extend their own influence over the land. They give the Meduvians the cult sites where the paladins of each side can summon mighty creatures to fight the other side.\par
But there were also some wise mages in Meduvia who kept out of the fighting and wanted to try to halt the destruction. So in the year 118 they founded the great council of mages, which is called the Council of Cra-Kla-Zoth after its three founders. Through the divine power of the Holigon they create a magic staff that unites the energy of all four elements and forms the basis of the council's power.\par
But as this new authority begins to establish itself, the princes of the churches fear for their power. So in 120, despite their differences, they join forces to wipe the council from the world. They form the League of the Gods and, for the first time since the schism, pull together again.\par
Because there are repeated incidents and frictions within the League of the Gods, they do not manage to defeat the council. In 125 the council finally succeeds, through an ancient summoning ritual, in summoning the most magical of all beings, the dragon, and so at last in defeating the churches.\par
The two churches try to win the council over to their side and to ally with it against the other side. The council, however, wants to remain neutral, but leaves it to the trained magi whether, and if so for which side, they fight.\par
In 126, finally, comes the Peace of Cra-Kla-Zoth, which all three parties sign. With that, the war of faith is officially over.\par
